From 8869cf9c4f798e39b829c9c805b7acf4cec05e67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:01:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(motion): 2D Adaptive keeps the full tool clear of "Do
 not touch" items

do_not_touch_applies accepts 2D Adaptive. The new module
machining2d::adaptive_avoid cuts the cutter-centre area back by one
full-tool keep-out (floor to clearance plane) and then runs the plain
planner over the reduced area: pocket_over_with_relief for Spiral,
trochoidal_inside for Trochoidal. The plain laws (crossing law, entry and
link certificates, the loops' confinement) read the reduced area. Rapid
links are lifted over the items; a link or a corner relief that cannot
clear them refuses the operation, and a region with no room left is
refused with the items named. Without protected items, or with a
keep-out off the region, the plain planner runs unchanged.

Pinned by motion avoid_adaptive, app do_not_touch_adaptive (one
heavy-lane case) and ui do_not_touch::adaptive2d_shows_the_pick_protected_button_and_no_unsupported_note.

Fixes #3346

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
